The '''New Republic Correctional Corps''' was a branch of the [[New Republic]] used to deal with [[prisoner]]s of the New Republic. The [[New Republic soldier]] [[Lieutenant]] [[Lant Davan]] was a member of the organization, which owned [[New Republic Correctional Transport]]s.<ref name="Chapter 10" />

{{Nr-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The New Republic Correctional Corps first appeared in "[[Chapter 6: The Prisoner]]" of [[Jon Favreau]]'s live-action television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', directed by [[Rick Famuyiwa]]<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> and released on [[December 13]], [[2019]] on [[Disney+]].<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|date=2019-09-24|format=[[Wikipedia:PDF|PDF]]|work=[[Wikipedia:Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International|Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]]|pages=[https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf#page=1]|archivedate=20210623202717}}</ref> The organization was later identified in "[[Chapter 10: The Passenger]]," which was directed by [[Peyton Reed]]<ref name="Chapter 10" /> and released on [[November 6]], [[2020]].<ref name="Chapter 10 date">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-november-2020|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in November 2020}}</ref>

